.TH geectl-update 1  "geectl-update 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-update \- Update the working copy in the current directory to the latest base
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl update\fR [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update the working copy in the current directory to the latest base
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
The revision to update to (a revision number or a srcmd5 (the source checksum of a revision, as `remote package\-log` reports it in JSON)). The latest when omitted
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
